notes=r'''The leaf has manuscript page 10 at the top and 12 at the lower left. It completes the component formulas (6.12)–(6.13) for Λ and presents eight conditions under (6.14). The slanted authorial note asks to prove that (iv) implies (ii), by proving π_i=π′_i, and ends with the underlined words “Démonstration à fournir.” That requested proof is left as a request in the transcription. The last sentence leads into simpler replacement formulas on the next leaf.

**N16-013-P1 — check of the two component formulas.** Write r=i−2α and use the page’s component map p↦L^αp from P^r to M^i. On its image the right side of (6.12) sends L^αp to L^(α−1)w_rL^(n−i+2α)p=L^(α−1)p. The projector kills the other components. On the upper component p↦L^(n−i+α)p, (6.13) sends that vector to L^(n−i+α−1)w_rL^(n−i+2α)p=L^(n−i+α−1)p. These are the stated lowering maps, with Λπ_i0=0. This calculation agrees with the visible α−1 in (6.12); H’s deletion of the L would remove the factor that returns the vector to the required component. The ink itself decides that live factor.

**N16-013-C1 — the displayed degree of Λ.** The remark visibly has Λ∈E^(2). On the explicit n=1 chain with basis a_0,a_2, L(a_0)=a_2, L(a_2)=0, and Λ(a_2)=a_0, Λ(a_0)=0, the map Λ has degree −2: its only nonzero component is Hom(M^2,M^0). Its degree +2 component is zero. The written +2 is retained. **N16-013-R1** records the computed degree −2 in this example and in the component maps of P1 (their output degree is the input degree minus 2); no minus sign is added to the source.

**N16-013-C2 — global identity in condition 3.** In the same n=1 chain take i=1, α=0. The middle space M^1 is zero, so π_1,0=0 and all π_1,α′ with α′>0 vanish. The right side of the written condition 3 is L^0Λ^0L^0·1=1 on the nonzero two-dimensional total space. Thus the global equality fails in this example. **N16-013-R2** is the component version already checked in N16-012-P1: replace the final factor by π_i−Σ_(α′>α)π_i,α′. The restriction homomorphism E^0→End(M^i), T↦T|M^i, sends π_i to the identity and gives exactly the written factor on M^i; the replacement kills every other graded component. In the explicit middle-degree example it makes both sides zero. The formula in the transcription remains 1−Σ.

**N16-013-C3 — index in condition 7.** The visible looped glyph is α, with a small upper retouch, in “si α≤n−1”; it is retained. At n=i=1, α=0, that written range admits the factor L^(−1), while the explicit L above is nilpotent and has no inverse. **N16-013-R3** records the actual range i≤n−1 in the preceding (6.13); there the exponent n−i+α−1 is nonnegative for the component indices α≥0. This is a comparison with the author’s earlier formula, not an emendation of condition 7.

The deleted projector in (6.13), the little cancelled alpha by π_i, the right-margin cancellation, the old w-index in condition 3, and the isolated cancelled alpha after condition 5 remain uncertain. The last of these was visible in the half; its tight crop clips its upper tip and does not settle the uncertainty. The two cancelled endpoint projectors in condition 2 are readable on their shared crop.''' 
